# Bing tile cache and the mosaic built from it. 36 MB, and entirely reproducible
# by rerunning tools/georef2.py. It is a cache, not a source.
tools/tilecache/
tools/ref_mosaic.jpg

# Proof sheets and debug renders. Regenerate with validate.py / residual.py /
# extract_annotations.py. Kept out because they are large and derived, but note
# that annot_check.jpg and georef_check*.jpg are the evidence behind the
# georeference, so regenerate them before trusting any change to it.
tools/*_check.jpg
tools/*_preview.png
tools/dbg_*.png
tools/cmp_*.jpg

# Solved transforms and control points. Derived from refine.py / georef_annot.py.
# georef.json is deliberately NOT ignored: web/index.html's bounds come from it
# and the numbers need to be reviewable in the diff.
tools/*.npy
tools/georef_annot.json

# Saved copies of the live Squarespace site, 2.6 MB of framework noise. They are
# a snapshot of somebody else's site, refetchable, and they go stale.
docs/site-revamp/_*.html

# Source imagery lives in Downloads and is far too large to version.
*.psd

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
dist/
tools/*check*.jpg

# Python bytecode and remaining debug renders from the failed georeferencing runs
__pycache__/
*.pyc
tools/align_overlay.png
tools/mask_ref.png
tools/dbg_*.jpg
gl.json

# Extracted copy: derived from the saved Squarespace HTML, which is itself
# ignored. Regenerate with tools/extract_site_copy.py.
tools/site_copy.json
tools/copy_preview.txt

# The map is copied into the site tree at build time so the whole thing is
# navigable locally; in production it deploys separately.
site/mapa/app/

# Rendered annotated sheets. Four PNGs, 9.9 MB, regenerated in one command by
# tools/render_annotated.py from coastline.json plus the tile cache. Kept out of
# a PUBLIC repo for the size; coastline.json IS tracked, because it is the
# geometry the sheets and the map both depend on and it needs to be reviewable.
# They live in out/ and NOT in web/, because web/ is dragged into Cloudflare
# Pages whole and these are unsigned drafts.
out/

# The satellite tile pyramid. 2,152 files and ~20 MB, rebuilt in one command by
# tools/build_tiles.py from the z17 cache plus a fetch of the low zooms. A PUBLIC
# repository is the wrong place to keep twenty megabytes of third-party imagery,
# and the build is deterministic, so the bytes are not worth versioning.
# NOTE: docs/deploy-cloudflare-pages.md opens by telling a deployer to run that
# command first, because deploying without it yields a map with no imagery and
# no warning. Keep those two facts in step.
web/tiles/
dist-map/
